  "result": "It returns **0.13** (13%).\n\n- `QuantityDiscount(60)` gives 0.05, since 60 falls in the 10 to 49 band... no, the 50 to 99 band, which gives 0.10.\n\nCorrecting that: `QuantityDiscount` checks `>= 50` first, so 60 gives **0.10**. The total is 0.10 + 0.03 (loyalty, 3 × 0.01) + 0.05 (Nonprofit) = **0.18**.\n\nSo `CombinedDiscount(60, 3, \"Nonprofit\")` returns **0.18m** (18%).\n\nThe Nonprofit check is an exact, case-sensitive string comparison (`customerType == \"Nonprofit\"`), so `\"nonprofit\"` would not add the 0.05. Source: `backend\\src\\InvoiceApp.Domain\\DiscountCalculator.cs:19-29`.",
